-- title:
--   Toric 𝔪-torsion bound at p∈𝔪
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ whose nonunits contain $p$ (the predicate [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16)), level data $\Lambda$ of level $N_0$ at $p$ over $A$ satisfying `LevelData.IsJacobian` (so that $\Lambda$ is a commutative relative group scheme over the base at $p$ with abelian-scheme bundle property, whose generic and special points identify with $J_0(N_0)$ and its reduction compatibly with the Galois and Hecke actions), and an object $O$ of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, i.e. a smooth separated surjective commutative relative group scheme over the base at $p$ whose generic fibre points are identified with $J_0(N_0p)=$ `JZero (N₀ * p)` (the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $N_0p$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$), equipped with Galois and Hecke compatibilities, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, proper generic fibre and toric data. Assume further $p\neq 2$; that `HeckeInputsAll (N₀ * p)` holds, i.e. `HeckeInputsAlong` holds at every prime $\ell$; that the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ at level $N_0p$ commute pairwise; and that $\mathfrak m$ is a maximal ideal of $\mathbb T=$ `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbf Z[X_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ which is not eventually Eisenstein (there is no finite set $S$ of primes with $T_\ell-(\ell+1)\in\mathfrak m$ for all $\ell\notin S$), contains $p$, has finite residue field $k=\mathbb T/\mathfrak m$, and is such that the $\mathfrak m$-torsion $J_0(N_0p)[\mathfrak m]$ (the $\mathfrak m$-torsion submodule for the module structure `heckeModuleBar (N₀ * p)`) has $k$-dimension $2$. The conclusion is that the intersection of the subgroup `O.toricPts p` of $J_0(N_0p)$ — the subgroup generated by the image of $O$'s toric points at $p$ — with the additive subgroup underlying $J_0(N_0p)[\mathfrak m]$ has cardinality at most $\#k$.
--
--   This is the multiplicity bound on the toric part of the $\mathfrak m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0p)$ at a prime $p$ lying in $\mathfrak m$, the group-theoretic form of the statement that the character group $X$ of the toric part of the reduction satisfies $\dim_k X/\mathfrak m X\le 1$; it is one of the inputs to the construction of the ordinary data used in the level-lowering step at $p$, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_of_children_of_neronExtension`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_of_children_of_neronExtension).
